# SersicPhotometry
# SersicCatSDSS
# v09
# 2015-12-17
# Lee Kelvin <l.s.kelvin@ljmu.ac.uk>
#
# This table provides the results of a single-Sersic-component fit to
# the 2D surface brightness distribution of every object in the
# GAMA II equatorial survey regions in the SDSS ugriz bands.
#
CATAID             1  -             meta.id                                            GAMA Object ID
RA                 2  deg           pos.eq.ra                                          Right Ascension (J2000)
DEC                3  deg           pos.eq.dec                                         Declination (J2000)
R_PETRO            4  mag           phot.mag;em.opt.R                                  Extinction-corrected SDSS DR7 Petrosian mag
SURVEY_OLDCLASS    5  -             meta.code.class                                    Useful for selecting samples, see notes
SURVEY_CLASS       6  -             meta.code.class                                    Useful for selecting samples, see notes
CENFLUX_u          7  counts        phot.count;em.opt.u                                Central pixel flux value prior to background estimation
BACKFLUX_u         8  counts        phot.count;em.opt.u                                SEx subtracted background at object position      
PSFNUM_u           9  -             meta.number;em.opt.u                               PSFEx number of stars used
PSFCHI2_u         10  -             stat.fit.goodness;em.opt.u                         PSFEx PSF reduced Chi^2
PSFFWHM_u         11  arcsec        instr.det.psf;meta.modelled;em.opt.u               PSFEx PSF FWHM
NSEC_u            12  -             meta.number;em.opt.u                               SEx number of secondary components detected
GALXCEN_u         13  pixel         pos.cartesian.x;meta.modelled;em.opt.u             GALFIT pixel pos. of model in cutout (x)
GALYCEN_u         14  pixel         pos.cartesian.y;meta.modelled;em.opt.u             GALFIT pixel pos. of model in cutout (y)
GALMAG_u          15  mag           phot.mag;meta.modelled;em.opt.u                    GALFIT magnitude of Sersic model
GALRE_u           16  arcsec        phys.angSize;meta.modelled;em.opt.u                GALFIT effective (half-light) radius (semi-major axis)
GALINDEX_u        17  -             stat.fit.param;meta.modelled;em.opt.u              GALFIT Sersic index
GALELLIP_u        18  -             src.ellipticity;meta.modelled;em.opt.u             GALFIT ellipticity (1-(b/a))
GALPA_u           19  deg           pos.posAng;meta.modelled;em.opt.u                  GALFIT position angle (x+, CCW) (see notes)
GALXCENERR_u      20  pixel         pos.cartesian.x;stat.error;meta.modelled;em.opt.u  GALFIT error on x position
GALYCENERR_u      21  pixel         pos.cartesian.y;stat.error;meta.modelled;em.opt.u  GALFIT error on y position
GALMAGERR_u       22  mag           phot.mag;stat.error;meta.modelled;em.opt.u         GALFIT error on magnitude
GALREERR_u        23  arcsec        phys.angSize;stat.error;meta.modelled;em.opt.u     GALFIT error on re
GALINDEXERR_u     24  -             stat.fit.param;stat.error;meta.modelled;em.opt.u   GALFIT error on Sersic index
GALELLIPERR_u     25  -             src.ellipticity;stat.error;meta.modelled;em.opt.u  GALFIT error on ellipticity
GALPAERR_u        26  deg           pos.posAng;stat.error;meta.modelled;em.opt.u       GALFIT error on position angle
GALRA_u           27  deg           pos.eq.ra;meta.modelled;em.opt.u                   GALFIT Right Ascension as determined by GALFIT
GALDEC_u          28  deg           pos.eq.dec;meta.modelled;em.opt.u                  GALFIT Declination as determined by GALFIT
GALMAG10RE_u      29  mag           phot.mag;meta.modelled;em.opt.u                    GALFIT magnitude of model, truncated at 10*re
GALMU0_u          30  mag/arcsec^2  phot.mag.sb;meta.modelled;em.opt.u                 GALFIT central surface brightness
GALMUE_u          31  mag/arcsec^2  phot.mag.sb;meta.modelled;em.opt.u                 GALFIT effective surface brightness at re
GALMUEAVG_u       32  mag/arcsec^2  phot.mag.sb;meta.modelled;em.opt.u                 GALFIT effective surface brightness within re
GALR90_u          33  arcsec        phys.angSize;meta.modelled;em.opt.u                GALFIT rad containing 90% of total light (semi-major axis)
GALCHI2FULL_u     34  -             stat.fit.goodness;em.opt.u                         GALFIT Chi^2 goodness-of-fit parameter (pri + sec)
GALNDOF_u         35  -             stat.fit.goodness;em.opt.u                         GALFIT model number of degrees of freedom (pri + sec)
GALCHI2_u         36  -             stat.fit.goodness;em.opt.u                         GALFIT reduced Chi^2 of output model (pri + sec)
GALPLAN_u         37  -             stat.fit.goodness;em.opt.u                         SIGMA chosen GALFIT modelling plan (see notes)
PRICHI2FULL_u     38  -             stat.fit.goodness;em.opt.u                         PRIMARY Chi^2 goodness-of-fit paramter (primary only)
PRINFP_u          39  -             stat.fit.goodness;em.opt.u                         PRIMARY model number of free parameters (primary only)
PRINDOF_u         40  -             stat.fit.goodness;em.opt.u                         PRIMARY model number of degrees of freedom (primary only)
PRICHI2_u         41  -             stat.fit.goodness;em.opt.u                         PRIMARY reduced Chi^2 of output model (primary only)
